WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.550
Bag Remake Studio in Shonan, Japan,

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.273
repairs designer bags and accessories.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.490
This $800 monogram wallet

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.640
is an unmistakable Louis Vuitton staple.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.150
The owner uses it on a daily basis,

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.390
and now the lining is deteriorating,

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:26.970
the leather is discolored,

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.680
and the paint is peeling on the edges.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.220
One of the studios repairmen will show us

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.030
how they restore this wallet

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.910
by taking it apart, repainting it,

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:40.813
creating new linings, and
stitching it all back together.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.130
First, the artist takes the bag apart

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.743
in order to work on each piece separately.

00:00:54.874 --> 00:00:57.291
(soft music)

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:01.993
He uses a seam ripper to
carefully take out the thread.

00:01:06.411 --> 00:01:08.828
(soft music)

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.720
After he takes off the
outer shell of the wallet,

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.023
he uses a sewing awl to take
out the internal threads.

00:01:20.191 --> 00:01:22.608
(soft music)

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.140
Next, he'll move on to fixing

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.113
the severely discolored leather.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:48.240
He starts by color matching
the brown shade of the wallet.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.130
This shade is made by
combining black, yellow, red,

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.743
and white leather paints.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:59.930
Once he has a perfect match,

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:02.720
he uses a paintbrush
to slowly start coating

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.520
the discolored parts of the leather.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.410
He won't touch the signature monogram.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:13.053
This preserves the
authenticity of the piece.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.260
After years of rubbing against money,

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.943
the interior lining needs to be replaced.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:31.013
The customer requested a nylon lining.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:37.290
To do this, the repairman
cuts out the new lining

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.420
with a sharp knife,

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.233
using the exterior of
the wallet as a stencil.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:49.570
He coats the wallet in glue

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:53.153
and presses the new
lining onto each piece.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:01.343
Once the piece is dry, they are
ready to come back together.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.130
The artisan sews them slowly,

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:08.990
carefully ensuring each stitch
goes into the exact same hole

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:10.093
as the original.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:19.230
Once the three main pieces
of the wallet are assembled,

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.873
the artisan glues and sews them together.

00:03:24.466 --> 00:03:26.883
(soft music)

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.390
To finish this repair,

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:45.030
he paints the edges of the
wallet where it's peeling

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.003
with an edge coat.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:51.973
This ensures that all of the
wallet's corners are sealed.

00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:56.606
(soft music)

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:05.560
The final step is to
hand rub the whole wallet

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:06.690
with mink oil,

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.700
which will prevent the
leather from peeling

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.280
or getting discolored

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:13.863
and will extend its
life for years to come.

